:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #e6e6e6; } }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 1.0 (build 1000)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Licenses from requests.</b> The Review Manager opens with a <i>Requests</i> section: everyone waiting for a Mac app license, amber, with <b>Issue License…</b> on each. The license window comes prefilled, offers 1, 3 or 6 months, and after saving writes the letter for you &#8212; <b>Send by Mail…</b> hands Mail the message with the file attached and the download link for the app you pick; <b>Copy Letter</b> when there is no mail client.</li>
<li>The license window is its own window now, above the floating panels that used to bury it.</li>
<li>Extension requests from an expired Asobi Review arrive in the same place.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
